From 6cfb73bfe44913ac9ad7cf06888d3fc239b4a7b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:28:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: rcar: support the RZ/V2H(P) and RZ/V2N USBHS

The legacy USBHS port knew only R-Car Gen3 and RZ/G2L addresses; on
RZ/V2N it poked R-Car clock registers and the R-Car controller base.

RZ/V2H(P)/V2N (CONFIG_R9A09G057/056) use the RZ/G2L USBHS at 0x15820000
with the USB2 PHY at 0x15800200. U-Boot's CPG driver for them does not
gate clocks, so release the USB2.0 clocks, bus master stops and resets
directly, initialise the USB2PHY control block as Linux'
reset-rzv2h-usb2phy does, and set up the PHY as Linux'
phy-rcar-gen3-usb2 does for these SoCs (no ADP block, UTMI control),
always in peripheral mode. Also fix two always-true guards.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
